# `math/round` answers `none` for NaN and the infinities on every engine,
# `math/round!` answers a failure in its box, and a call passing an int is
# typed int alone (ruled 2026-09-29). Each row puts one of the five back.
nonfinite_native = row
  "a non-finite float rounded to zero natively"
  true
  "cargo test --release --test golden micro_corpus_agrees_across_engines"
  "specs (unit, golden, differential)"
  (breaking "a_non_finite_float_rounded_to_zero_natively")
